{
  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted, acc=0.725) combines all individually best components. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the 200-dim scvi bottleneck vs. 2000-dim PCA representation interacts differently with the strong ViT image encoder in the multimodal setting. In rna_only, scvi_n200 (0.520) beat pca_n2000 (0.485) by ~0.035, but with a powerful image modality providing complementary spatial information, the higher-dimensional PCA may retain gene-level detail that the 200-dim scvi bottleneck discards. Config_027 changes only the RNA encoder (scvi_n200→pca_n2000) while holding all other settings at their empirically best values, making it a clean single-variable comparison against config_039. It is the highest-expected-value untested configuration and the most informative final experiment: if it approaches or exceeds 0.725, it reveals a meaningful encoder×modality interaction; if it falls short, it confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal RNA representation in the multimodal regime."
}

